{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A stubborn and rebellious son.</b> According to the opinion of our Sages (Sanhedrin 71), he is not a minor, for a minor is exempt from all punishments in the Torah and from all commandments; rather, he is one who has brought two pubic hairs. Now there are two transgressions upon him: the first, that he treats his father and mother lightly and is rebellious against them; and the second, that he is a glutton and a drunkard, thereby transgressing what we were commanded (Leviticus 19:2), \"You shall be holy,\" and it is further stated (Deuteronomy 13:5), \"Him you shall serve and to Him you shall cleave,\" as I explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 6:13) that we were commanded to know HaShem in all our ways, and a glutton and a drunkard does not know the way of HaShem. In general, there is in him at present no capital offense, and he is judged on account of his eventual end, as our Sages mentioned (Sanhedrin 71). This is the reason for \"and all Israel shall hear and fear\" (Deuteronomy 21:21) — for he is not put to death because of the magnitude of his sin, but rather to discipline the multitudes through him, so that he will not become a stumbling block to others. And so is the way of Scripture to give such a warning when they put someone to death: to make a fence, so that through their death there will be a correction for others. For it mentions the same in the case of the rebellious elder (Deuteronomy 17:13), because there is no capital offense in his ruling that would make him worthy of death for it; rather, it is to remove schism from the Torah, as I explained there (Ramban on Deuteronomy 17:11). And likewise in the case of conspiring witnesses (Deuteronomy 19:20), who are executed though they did not kill anyone; and likewise it mentions the same in the case of the inciter (Deuteronomy 13:12), because he is executed for his evil speech alone, even though the enticed person did not serve idolatry and did not listen to him — rather, his execution is to discipline those who remain. And this too is a new commandment, or one that elucidates \"Honor your father and your mother\" (Exodus 20:12) and \"Every one of you shall fear his mother and his father\" (Leviticus 19:3)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The citation of Ramban on Deuteronomy 17:11 appears in the Hebrew text with the verse number 21:11, which is evidently a typographical error for 17:11, the passage on the rebellious elder; the translation renders the corrected reference silently."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:53:10.780468385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}